                desc:
                  '''
                  Whether or not the ROM should use the NVM (flash or RRAM)
                  ECC exception handler during execution. A value of
                  kHardenedBoolTrue allows the ROM to use the exception
                  handler that recovers gracefully and continues the boot
                  process if an NVM ECC error is encountered during
                  verification of a specific ROM_EXT slot. This enables the
                  ROM to attempt booting the next ROM_EXT slot if the first
                  slot attempted has been corrupted. All other values
                  trigger default ROM exception handling, which is all
                  exceptions trigger a chip shutdown and reset.
